From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] pdf: Pass vertical glyph advances with the sign that
 fitz uses.

In vertical writing mode a PDF font gives the advance of a glyph as w1
(from W2 or DW2), which is negative when the text goes down (the default
is -1000). pdf_show_char passed it on unchanged, but fitz expects a
vertical advance to be positive for text that goes down: fz_show_string
moves the pen by -adv and fz_advance_glyph returns the positive vertical
advance of the font. So the structured text device put the start of
every vertical character one em below its end, found the next character
two ems away and started a new line for it: every character of a
vertical column became a line of its own, its box covered the em below
the glyph origin, mostly over the next character, and selecting,
copying and searching more than one character failed on vertical text.
The advance of a vertical glyph is now negated before it goes into the
text object. Drawing does not use the advance, so the rendering stays
the same.

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-20.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/pdf/pdf-op-run.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/pdf/pdf-op-run.c b/source/pdf/pdf-op-run.c
index 5ef4ccf..55be8e3 100644
--- a/source/pdf/pdf-op-run.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-op-run.c
@@ -1361,6 +1361,11 @@ pdf_show_char(fz_context *ctx, pdf_run_processor *pr, int cid, fz_text_language
 
 	gid = pdf_tos_make_trm(ctx, &pr->tos, &gstate->text, fontdesc, cid, &trm, &adv);
 
+	/* A PDF vertical advance is negative when the text goes down, but
+	 * fitz expects it positive then, like fz_advance_glyph gives it. */
+	if (fontdesc->wmode)
+		adv = -adv;
+
 	/* If we are uncachable, then render direct. */
 	render_direct = !fz_glyph_cacheable(ctx, fontdesc->font, gid);
 
